{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"dc075b0e44875c49ed577d570c01cdcfcb91a3e255432a9d08b032f9b5a7e517","digest":{"component_or_area":"test infrastructure / repo-isolation session hooks","key_entities":["tests/_isolation.py","pytest_sessionfinish","_no_repo_commits","GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS","porcelain()","head()","git rev-parse HEAD","git status --porcelain","subprocess.TimeoutExpired","tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py"],"problem_keywords":["git probe timeout","subprocess hanging","test isolation","pytest session hooks","unbounded process"],"propositions":["Git probes in repo-isolation session hooks (`porcelain()` and `head()`) run synchronously without a subprocess timeout, allowing a blocked child process to keep pytest alive indefinitely after test completion.","The root cause affects both `pytest_sessionfinish` hook and the autouse `_no_repo_commits` per-test fixture, both invoking read-only Git status checks without a watchdog.","Timeout errors must be explicitly surfaced as isolation-infrastructure failures (re-raising `subprocess.TimeoutExpired`) while preserving `None` for ordinary probe failures (non-repository, OSError, SubprocessError).","A fixed 5-second `GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` watchdog is sufficient, providing >80x headroom over measured probe latencies (p95: 0.0164s, max: 0.0610s for 100 normal probes)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787072355504692001,"uuid":"31b2ce62-fc51-41da-aa8d-0553608ce49a"}